			"index": "aY",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 320719059,
			"version": 314,
			"versionNonce": 2063460275,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1772131402480,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1404. Number of Steps to Reduce a\nNumber in Binary Representation to One",
			"fontSize": 36,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1404. Number of Steps to Reduce a\nNumber in Binary Representation to One",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "wupUWWle",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1044.4532015100358,
			"y": 420.553672686705,
			"width": 570.3125,
			"height": 475,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "aZ",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1559164467,
			"version": 748,
			"versionNonce": 120327603,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1772131639142,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "given the binary representation of an integer as a string `s`\nreturn the number of steps to reduce it to 1 following these rules:\n- if the current number is even, you have to divide it by 2\n- if the current number is odd, you have to add 1 to it\n\nit is guaranteed that you can always reach one for all test cases\n\ne.g. 1\ninput: s = \"1101\"\noutput: 6\n\nexplanation: \"1101\" corresponds to 13\n- let n = 13, the decimal value of the bin s string\n- step 1: 13 is odd, add 1, n = 14\n- step 2: 14 is even, divide by 2, n = 7\n- step 3: 7 is odd, add 1, n = 8\n- step 4: 8 is even, divide by 2, n = 4\n- step 5: 4 is even, divide by 2, n = 2\n- step 6: 2 is even, divide by 2, n = 1",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "given the binary representation of an integer as a string `s`\nreturn the number of steps to reduce it to 1 following these rules:\n- if the current number is even, you have to divide it by 2\n- if the current number is odd, you have to add 1 to it\n\nit is guaranteed that you can always reach one for all test cases\n\ne.g. 1\ninput: s = \"1101\"\noutput: 6\n\nexplanation: \"1101\" corresponds to 13\n- let n = 13, the decimal value of the bin s string\n- step 1: 13 is odd, add 1, n = 14\n- step 2: 14 is even, divide by 2, n = 7\n- step 3: 7 is odd, add 1, n = 8\n- step 4: 8 is even, divide by 2, n = 4\n- step 5: 4 is even, divide by 2, n = 2\n- step 6: 2 is even, divide by 2, n = 1",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "QFMXJPfpF8-yiBvZfGPLi",
