			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773547629769,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "You are given two integer arrays nums1 and nums2, sorted in \nnon-decreasing order, and two integers m and n, representing the\nnumber of elements in nums1 and nums2 respectively.\n\nMerge nums1 and nums2 into a single array sorted in \nnon-decreasing order.\n\nThe final sorted array should not be returned by the function,\nbut instead be stored inside the array nums1. To accommodate\nthis, nums1 has a length of m + n, where the first m elements\ndenote the elements that should be merged, and the last \nn elements are set to 0 and should be ignored. nums2 has a \nlength of n.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "You are given two integer arrays nums1 and nums2, sorted in \nnon-decreasing order, and two integers m and n, representing the\nnumber of elements in nums1 and nums2 respectively.\n\nMerge nums1 and nums2 into a single array sorted in \nnon-decreasing order.\n\nThe final sorted array should not be returned by the function,\nbut instead be stored inside the array nums1. To accommodate\nthis, nums1 has a length of m + n, where the first m elements\ndenote the elements that should be merged, and the last \nn elements are set to 0 and should be ignored. nums2 has a \nlength of n.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
