		{
			"id": "GOacXoQE",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 4800.19224530312,
			"y": 3852.4928446145277,
			"width": 580.9765625,
			"height": 400,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b5M",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 2131478578,
			"version": 451,
			"versionNonce": 2019975214,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773547629770,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Given an integer array nums sorted in non-decreasing order,\nremove some duplicates in-place such that each unique element\nappears at most twice. The relative order of the elements should\nbe kept the same.\n\nSince it is impossible to change the length of the array in some\nlanguages, you must instead have the result be placed in the first\npart of the array nums. More formally, if there are k elements after\nremoving the duplicates, then the first k elements of nums should\nhold the final result. It does not matter what you leave beyond the\nfirst k elements.\n\nReturn k after placing the final result in the first k slots of nums.\n\nDo not allocate extra space for another array. You must do this by\nmodifying the input array in-place with O(1) extra memory.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Given an integer array nums sorted in non-decreasing order,\nremove some duplicates in-place such that each unique element\nappears at most twice. The relative order of the elements should\nbe kept the same.\n\nSince it is impossible to change the length of the array in some\nlanguages, you must instead have the result be placed in the first\npart of the array nums. More formally, if there are k elements after\nremoving the duplicates, then the first k elements of nums should\nhold the final result. It does not matter what you leave beyond the\nfirst k elements.\n\nReturn k after placing the final result in the first k slots of nums.\n\nDo not allocate extra space for another array. You must do this by\nmodifying the input array in-place with O(1) extra memory.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "EveurNL7",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 4798.000950662277,
			"y": 4318.177470152939,
			"width": 608.623046875,
			"height": 350,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b5N",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1507722094,
			"version": 458,
			"versionNonce": 1363552878,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773547629770,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Custom Judge:\n\nThe judge will test your solution with the following code:\n\nint[] nums = [...]; // Input array\nint[] expectedNums = [...]; // The expected answer with correct length\n\nint k = removeDuplicates(nums); // Calls your implementation\n\nassert k == expectedNums.length;\nfor (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n    assert nums[i] == expectedNums[i];\n}\nIf all assertions pass, then your solution will be accepted.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Custom Judge:\n\nThe judge will test your solution with the following code:\n\nint[] nums = [...]; // Input array\nint[] expectedNums = [...]; // The expected answer with correct length\n\nint k = removeDuplicates(nums); // Calls your implementation\n\nassert k == expectedNums.length;\nfor (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n    assert nums[i] == expectedNums[i];\n}\nIf all assertions pass, then your solution will be accepted.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "BkNSd4IX",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 4796.020027571736,
			"y": 4754.405734728686,
			"width": 557.91015625,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b5O",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 561526130,
			"version": 453,
			"versionNonce": 137538734,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1773547629770,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Example 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,1,1,2,2,3]\nOutput: 5, nums = [1,1,2,2,3,_]\nExplanation: Your function should return k = 5, with the first five\nelements of nums being 1, 1, 2, 2 and 3 respectively.\nIt does not matter what you leave beyond the\nreturned k (hence they are underscores).",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Example 1:\n\nInput: nums = [1,1,1,2,2,3]\nOutput: 5, nums = [1,1,2,2,3,_]\nExplanation: Your function should return k = 5, with the first five\nelements of nums being 1, 1, 2, 2 and 3 respectively.\nIt does not matter what you leave beyond the\nreturned k (hence they are underscores).",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "EUZJLucD",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 4795.49271581299,
			"y": 5022.6273856541175,
			"width": 580.15625,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
