			"updated": 1774574373089,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. get a number\n2. look for a number that equals target - nums[i] (for this array))\n1, -1, 0, 0, -2, 2    is one way to make output[0]\n\n-2, -1, 0, 0, -1, 1   however, output[0] and the others seem\nto be sorted, let's try sorting the nums array first",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1. get a number\n2. look for a number that equals target - nums[i] (for this array))\n1, -1, 0, 0, -2, 2    is one way to make output[0]\n\n-2, -1, 0, 0, -1, 1   however, output[0] and the others seem\nto be sorted, let's try sorting the nums array first",
