		{
			"id": "iyoxDTkO",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 9651.53492134206,
			"y": 8599.769938117672,
			"width": 543.6328125,
			"height": 125,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bNe",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 793334806,
			"version": 5,
			"versionNonce": 464230678,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1774576341546,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Given an integer array nums, return all the triplets \n[nums[i], nums[j], nums[k]] such that i != j, i != k, and j != k, \nand nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0.\n\nNotice that the solution set must not contain duplicate triplets.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Given an integer array nums, return all the triplets \n[nums[i], nums[j], nums[k]] such that i != j, i != k, and j != k, \nand nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0.\n\nNotice that the solution set must not contain duplicate triplets.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "nD0w4zkY",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 9658.101961898079,
			"y": 8779.533545687762,
			"width": 440.1953125,
			"height": 275,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#ffffff",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bNf",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 105078294,
			"version": 29,
			"versionNonce": 573312586,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1774576361176,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Example 1:\n\nInput: nums = [-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]\nOutput: [[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]\nExplanation: \nnums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2] = (-1) + 0 + 1 = 0.\nnums[1] + nums[2] + nums[4] = 0 + 1 + (-1) = 0.\nnums[0] + nums[3] + nums[4] = (-1) + 2 + (-1) = 0.\nThe distinct triplets are [-1,0,1] and [-1,-1,2].\nNotice that the order of the output and the order\nof the triplets does not matter.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Example 1:\n\nInput: nums = [-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]\nOutput: [[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]\nExplanation: \nnums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2] = (-1) + 0 + 1 = 0.\nnums[1] + nums[2] + nums[4] = 0 + 1 + (-1) = 0.\nnums[0] + nums[3] + nums[4] = (-1) + 2 + (-1) = 0.\nThe distinct triplets are [-1,0,1] and [-1,-1,2].\nNotice that the order of the output and the order\nof the triplets does not matter.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "XQxZYh22",
